-- title:
--   The upper bound $\#\mathrm{Hom}(I(Q), \mathbb{Z}/N) \le N$ for inertia at a boundary prime
-- statement:
--   In a Dedekind domain, $N \mid v(x)$ gives $x s = c^N b$ with $b, s \notin v$. Elements of $K_U$ lying in the field generated by $\Gamma$-fixed elements are $\Gamma$-fixed. The main result is a pigeonhole statement: among any $N + 1$ locally constant homomorphisms $I(Q) \to \mathbb{Z}/N$ on the inertia group of a nonzero prime $Q$ of the pro-chart, two coincide (via Kummer theory, the valuation mod $N$ of the radicands at $Q \cap R_0$, and the local Kummer lemma). Hence if one character $\theta$ is onto, every locally constant homomorphism $\chi : I(Q) \to \mathbb{Z}/N$ is $$\chi = k\,\theta \quad \text{for a unique } k \in \mathbb{Z}/N.$$
--
--   **Formalization note.** Library module of a formalization of the Ramanujan-Petersson conjecture (etale fundamental groups, Kummer theory and tame ramification on affine curves over finite fields). It contains definitions together with proved lemmas (no `sorry`), so that later solution files can import them.
-- source:
--   J.-P. Serre, Local Fields, GTM 67, Springer (1979), Chapter IV, Section 2; A. Grothendieck, J. P. Murre, The Tame Fundamental Group of a Formal Neighbourhood of a Divisor with Normal Crossings on a Scheme, Lecture Notes in Math. 208, Springer (1971)

